{
  "name": "iOS \u2014 Screen Load Timings",
  "tabs": [
    {
      "name": "Screen loads",
      "stylistic_components": [
        {
          "id": "t-intro-h",
          "text_component": {
            "text": "iOS \u2014 how long does each screen take to load?",
            "variant": "h2"
          },
          "dashboard_layout_settings": {
            "x": 0,
            "y": 0,
            "column_span": 12,
            "row_span": 3
          }
        },
        {
          "id": "t-intro-p",
          "text_component": {
            "text": "Standalone root spans (not nested under any journey span) wrapping each screen's `.task` data fetch \u2014 see `welcome_screen_load`'s comment in Screens.swift for why they aren't nested. Because workflow matching runs on-device against every span as it's emitted, these are exact per-session numbers, not a sample. `catalog_serialize` runs on every Browse load regardless of Rec v2 \u2014 the flag only gates whether the resulting string goes on to be consumed; `product_image_load` fires once per visible product thumbnail, so a screen with N rows contributes N samples. See bd-shop-21 in workflows/.",
            "variant": "p"
          },
          "dashboard_layout_settings": {
            "x": 0,
            "y": 3,
            "column_span": 12,
            "row_span": 8
          }
        }
      ],
